export anchor VinylLoungeStyle:
    number: 326
    screen: MusicPlayer
    name: Vinyl lounge
    idea: A walnut turntable plinth fills half the screen with a spinning record drawn in SVG, a brass tonearm in the grooves, brass knobs for volume and a crate of record spines for the queue, all in warm serif type.
    base: dark
    palette:
        lounge: #1a110b, the page and the style sheet
        walnut: #2e1c11, the plinth, grained with walnutDark stripes
        walnutDark: #24160d, grain stripes, cards and the crate shelf
        groove: #121010, the record and inset wells
        cream: #f2e6cf, text and the record label
        parchment: #cdb795, artists, times and captions
        brass: #d9ab5f, the tonearm, knobs, engraved labels, the liked heart and rules
        onBrass: #26170a, glyphs and text on brass
        sleeve: #5a3b2a, one of five muted sleeve tints on the crate spines, decorative only
    type:
        One serif stack, Iowan Old Style, Palatino Linotype, Palatino, Book
        Antiqua, Georgia. Base 16px at 1.55. The title is 56px italic at
        400, the current lyric 22px, body 16px, engraved labels 12px at 600
        in caps with 0.2em tracking in brass, and times 14px with oldstyle
        figures.
    layout:
        Two columns on a lounge brown page. On the left a walnut plinth
        with a brass inlay line holds an engraved Brightwork Sound, Side A
        label and 33 rpm, then the turntable drawn in SVG, a black platter
        with fine grooves and a cream label reading Low Tide and SALTMARSH
        TRIO, slowly turning, with a brass tonearm from a round pivot
        resting in the outer grooves and a small pitch slider. A thin brass
        rail shows the elapsed and total time with a cream dot. A dark
        inset strip below holds three round brass buttons for previous, a
        larger pause and next, two slide switches labelled Shuffle Off and
        Repeat Off, and a brass rotary knob ringed by ticks pointing at 70
        with the word Volume. On the right sit the engraved Now spinning,
        the italic title, the artist with from Low Tide, and a pill
        reading Liked with a brass heart. Then a Liner notes card with a
        brass left edge shows the current line large behind a note sign
        and the next line in smaller italic. The crate lists the queue as
        record spines, each with a coloured sleeve edge, an italic brass
        number, title, artist and time. Shelves shows the three playlists
        as brass edged nameplates and underlined links for Albums, Artists
        and Podcasts. Below 980px the columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit used generously, 28px plinth padding and 24px between cards.
    density: Low. The turntable takes half the screen and every list stays short.
    corners: 12px plinth and cards, round knobs and buttons, 3px spines, 6px nameplates.
    borders: 1px brass hairlines at half strength on nameplates and the control strip, and a 2px brass inlay inside the plinth edge.
    shadows: A deep 0 18px 40px black under the plinth and small drop shadows under the brass buttons.
    icons:
        Solid glyphs engraved in dark brown on round brass buttons.
        Toggles are slide switches with the words Off or On beside them.
        The liked heart is filled brass beside the word Liked.
    focus: A 2px cream outline offset 3px with a 6px brass glow.
    tone: Lounge words, such as Now spinning, Side A, The crate, Liner notes and Shelves.
